WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.700
Tracing connects events across an AI workflow.

2
00:00:03.800 --> 00:00:18.360
A single user action may pass through a web interface, authentication layer, model router, retrieval service, vector store, document connector, tool approval step, local model server, output formatter, and audit service.

3
00:00:18.460 --> 00:00:23.500
Without correlation, each component sees only its own fragment of the story.

4
00:00:23.780 --> 00:00:27.460
Request IDs and correlation IDs make investigation possible.

5
00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:38.120
They help operators connect a user action to model calls, retrieval operations, tool calls, approval steps, retries, timeouts, and response status.

6
00:00:38.220 --> 00:00:44.780
A trace can show where latency occurred, which dependency failed, or why the workflow returned a degraded result.

7
00:00:45.060 --> 00:00:48.660
For private RAG systems, tracing should be privacy-aware.

8
00:00:48.760 --> 00:00:59.480
It can record which source groups were considered, which filters were applied, which documents or chunks were eligible, and how many were used without storing full sensitive content unnecessarily.

9
00:00:59.580 --> 00:01:04.700
The goal is to understand retrieval decisions without turning traces into another source copy.

10
00:01:04.980 --> 00:01:08.020
Context-window visibility is also important.

11
00:01:08.120 --> 00:01:18.520
Operators may need to know prompt size, retrieved material count, omitted context, truncation events, formatting failures, and whether a response had enough evidence.

12
00:01:18.620 --> 00:01:22.540
These signals help diagnose bad answers while preserving restraint.

13
00:01:22.820 --> 00:01:31.220
Tool-call traces should capture intent, target category, result status, approval state, and error category.

14
00:01:31.320 --> 00:01:34.600
They should not expose sensitive arguments by default.

15
00:01:34.700 --> 00:01:42.220
Good tracing makes sovereign AI workflows explainable while keeping the monitoring system aligned with privacy and governance boundaries.
